></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KYOGOKU, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOSHINO SUMIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO MASUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITO TAKEKIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KYOGOKU TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSHINO, SUMIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, MASUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITO, TAKEKIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KYOGOKU, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An interface region (20) is provided at the boundary between a core region (10) and a clad region (30). The refractive index of the interface region (20) decreases from the core region side toward the clad region side. The rate of change of relative index difference is found for the region where the relative index difference varies from 0.8x DELTA n to 0.3x DELTA n where  DELTA n is th        e relative index difference of the core region (10), and normalized by the radius  gamma  of the core. The normalized rate of change (0.5x DELTA n)/(d/ gamma ) is used as an index for evaluation of     the change of the refractive index. The lower limit of the allowable range of the normalized rate of change is determined to be 0.4%, and the upper limit thereof is determined to be 4.0%. The influence of the tailing of the profile of the refractive index and the strain in the optical fiber are reduced, thus providing a single-mode optical fiber through which low-loss optical transmission is possible.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Une région d'interface (20) est placée à la limite entre une partie coeur (10) et une partie gaine (30). L'indice de réfraction de la région d'interface (20) diminue de la face côté coeur vers la face côté gaine. Le taux de changement de la différence d'indice de réfraction est trouvé pour la région dans laquelle la différence d'indice relative varie de 0,8x DELTA n à 0,3x DELTA n,  DELTA n étant la différence d'indice relative de la région coeur (10), puis normalisé par le rayon  gamma  du coeur. Le taux de changement normalisé (0,5x DELTA n)/(d/ gamma ) est utilisé en tant qu'indice pour l'évaluation du changement de l'indice de réfraction. La limite inférieure de la gamme permise du taux de changement normalisé est déterminée comme étant 0,4 % et la limite supérieure est déterminée comme étant 4,0 %. L'influence de la variation du profil de l'indice de réfraction et la contrainte dans la fibre optique sont réduites, ce qui permet d'obtenir une fibre optique à mode unique par laquelle la transmission optique à faible perte est possible.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright><